<title>UK: Rugby pre-tax dips 19.7 pct in H1.</title>
<headline>Rugby pre-tax dips 19.7 pct in H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.0		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.5		    vs 1.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     29.0		   vs 36.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   590.2		  vs 540.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 26.5 to 28.5 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 30.3		   vs 36.0</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.3		    vs 0.1 receivable</p>
<p> Tax			  9.8		    vs 12.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		  19.2		   vs 23.5</p>
<p> Retained		   9.6		    vs 13.9</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 1</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1  Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Building materials company Rugby Group Plc said the outlook for the second half is mixed, adding there is no sign of recovery in the Australian housing market while improvement in the UK is only modest.</p>
<p>It said the improvement in the UK is largely offset by reductions in public infrastructure spending.</p>
<p>Rugby said its Cockburn and Pioneer units are expected to perform well and market conditions in the U.S. have improved. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
